THOUGHT: The error is that node.prev is annotated @Nullable, so dereferencing it directly in removeInternal triggers NullAway. From the Node constructor and header setup, prev should never be null for any node that’s actually in the linked list: the header’s prev is itself, and regular nodes are constructed with a non-null prev (header.prev) and immediately linked via prev.next = this. To satisfy NullAway without changing behavior, I can introduce local variables for prev and next, assert that prev is non-null, and then use the local variables for dereferences. This keeps runtime behavior the same but gives the checker more information. I’ll edit removeInternal accordingly and then rerun the NullAway build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/gson && sed -i '257,262s/node.prev.next = node.next;/Node<K, V> prev = node.prev;
      Node<K, V> next = node.next;
      if (prev == null) {
        throw new AssertionError("prev == null");
      }
      prev.next = next;/' gson/src/main/java/com/google/gson/internal/LinkedHashTreeMap.java && sed -i '260s/node.next.prev = node.prev;/next.prev = prev;/' gson/src/main/java/com/google/gson/internal/LinkedHashTreeMap.java && ./gradlew :gson:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 || true && tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

